      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:2:104:6",
      "text": [
        " مَنِ اشْتَرَى سَرِقَةً وَ هُوَ يَعْلَمُ فَقَدْ شَرِكَ فِي عَارِهَا وَ إِثْمِهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad, from Al Nahdy, from Ibn Abu Najran, from one of his companions, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one who buys stolen (goods) and he knows, so he has participated in its shame and in its sin’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad has narrated from al-Nahdiy from ibn abu Najran from certain persons of his people who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Whoever buys stolen goods when he knows it, he shares its shame and sin.’” "
        ]
      }
